{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on 1dd30c16 (Q-B1) and 72195ec5 for the cutover head\n(05d618e2). Q-B1 waited an hour. I set my read time three minutes\nlate at 22:33 and passed over your act of 22:29. That was my\nerror.\n\nQ-B1. Choose (a). This is the case that item 1e of b7c58915 told\nyou to stop on, and you stopped. An entry that records a use of a\nlater entry of a foreign sequence also records a use of that\nsequence's first entry. Each origin then proves its own uses, and\na replay needs nothing from outside the entry. Conditions:\n1. The rule is uniform. It holds for every entry kind that\n   records such a use, not for the reserve delivery alone.\n2. One birth use for each foreign sequence in one entry, however\n   many later entries of it the entry uses.\n3. The bytes come from the read that the entry already made. The\n   resolver returns the birth beside each source read. Ruling\n   222a5b21 holds: no read is added.\n4. The store keeps one copy of the birth bytes for one content\n   digest. Confirm that, or tell me that it does not.\n5. Check every cap at its charge site with the added use: the\n   uses of one entry, the bytes of one entry, the retained bytes\n   of a scope, and the observation caps. Put the numbers in the\n   note. If a cap cannot hold the added use, stop and name it.\n6. The vectors and the spec witnesses that state entry bytes\n   change in this head. List them in the note.\nDo not choose (b). A birth from another origin makes one entry\ndepend on another, and an archive floor can remove that other\nentry.\n\nQ-V1. Choose (a) for one case and (b) for the other. The\nreplay-mode case gets a genuinely sealed history whose genesis has\nthe wrong kind, so one test shows that replay refuses it with\n`genesis-kind`. The integrity-mode case expects the binding\nfailure and `mismatch`. One sealed fixture is enough.\n\nQ-V2. Decide after Q-B1 (a) is in. The origins then hold their\nbirths, and the two Weighing cases may read `consistent` again\nwith no change. If they still read `incomplete`, choose (a) and\nserve verified source histories.\n\nQ-C1. Choose (c). Keep the case with a damage that the new shape\ndetects, such as a wrong genesis. Add no projector rule.\n\nThe process note is accepted. Use WIP commits.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}